# Contract checkout portability (P026, Agent M-D — FreeBuff).
#
# Git stores the canonical contract blobs with LF endings, and the verification
# script hashes those files as RAW BYTES, so a clone whose Git configuration
# converts LF to CRLF on checkout fails the manifest hash checks even though the
# content is byte-identical apart from the line separator. Pinning LF for
# exactly the hashed paths keeps checkout portable without touching contract
# semantics, the manifest, or any verifier check. This is repository checkout
# configuration, not a contract version change; the same two rules are already
# committed in simulation-frontend and simulation-backend (K002).
contracts/v1/** text eol=lf
scripts/verify-contract.mjs text eol=lf
